-- title:
--   Proposition 6.1, p. 22 — the KŁ property of L_γ with exponent 1/2 at an accumulation point implies VP-EB
-- statement:
--   Let Assumptions 1 and 2 hold, let $\delta_k$ be set by (8), and let $\{w^k\}=\{(u^k,v^k,p^k)\}$ be generated by NAPP-AL. Let $\bar w$ be an accumulation point of $\{w^k\}$. Suppose the augmented Lagrangian $\mathcal L_\gamma$ has the Kurdyka–Łojasiewicz property at $\bar w$ with exponent $\theta=\tfrac12$: there are $\eta,\nu,\kappa_2>0$ with
--
--   $$\sqrt{\mathcal L_\gamma(x)-\mathcal L_\gamma(\bar w)}\le\kappa_2\operatorname{dist}\big(0,\partial\mathcal L_\gamma(x)\big)$$
--
--   for every $x$ with $\|x-\bar w\|<\eta$ and $\mathcal L_\gamma(\bar w)<\mathcal L_\gamma(x)<\mathcal L_\gamma(\bar w)+\nu$. Then the value proximity error bound holds at $\bar w$: there are $\kappa_1,\eta',\nu'>0$ such that
--
--   $$\mathcal L_\gamma(w^{k+1})-\mathcal L_\gamma(\bar w)\le\kappa_1\|w^k-w^{k+1}\|^2$$
--
--   for every $k$ with $\|w^{k+1}-\bar w\|<\eta'$ and $\mathcal L_\gamma(w^{k+1})<\mathcal L_\gamma(\bar w)+\nu'$.
--
--   Together with Theorem 5.1 of the paper, this shows that NAPP-AL converges linearly whenever $\mathcal L_\gamma$ has the KL property with exponent $\tfrac12$ at a cluster point.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The proposition says only "generated by NAPP-AL"; the hypotheses of Theorem 4.1 (Assumptions 1 and 2, and $\delta_k$ set by (8)) are the paper's standing setting and are used by the proof through Theorem 4.1(iv), so they are hypotheses here. The KL property uses the paper's set $\partial\mathcal L_\gamma$ of p. 6, with $\operatorname{dist}(0,\emptyset)=+\infty$; $\|\cdot\|$ on $(u,v,p)$ is the Euclidean norm of the stacked vector. VP-EB is the inequality of Definition 5.1 without that definition's presupposition that the sequence converges to $\bar w$; its constants are existential, as in the definition.
-- source:
--   Zhu, Zhao, Zhang, A First-Order Primal-Dual Method for Nonconvex Constrained Optimization Based on the Augmented Lagrangian, arXiv:2007.12219v1, p. 22, Proposition 6.1

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NAPPAL_KL_Setting

namespace NAPPAL.KL
theorem proposition_6_1 {n d m : ℕ} (P : Problem n d m) (LG LH L0 : ℝ) (LOmj : Fin m → ℝ)
    (LK : ℝ) (K : E n → ℝ) (β γ σ : ℝ) (δ ε : ℕ → ℝ) (u : ℕ → E n) (v : ℕ → E d)
    (p : ℕ → E m) (hrun : RunHyp P LG LH L0 LOmj LK K β γ σ δ ε u v p) (wbar : W n d m)
    (hcl : MapClusterPt wbar Filter.atTop (wseq u v p)) (η ν κ2 : ℝ)
    (hKL : HasKLAt P γ wbar (1 / 2) η ν κ2) :
    ∃ κ1 η' ν' : ℝ, VPEB P γ (wseq u v p) wbar κ1 η' ν' := by sorry
end NAPPAL.KL
